  "body": "## What changed\nA pick on a Probe op now seeds the op's mode, touch directions, expected contact and (for round picks) radius, inside the same undoable `SetOperationGeometry` command, so one Ctrl+Z takes back the pick and the seeded values together. `operation::probe_from_picks(...)` + `CreateOperation` with that pick as the source creates a seeded probe directly.\n- **Planar face:** Face touch against the face's outward normal (normal within 1 deg of +-X, +-Y or +Z). The target is the face centroid, or the nearest facet's centroid if the centroid falls in a hole.\n- **Straight level top edge:** Edge touch on the one vertical X/Y-facing wall under it; target is the edge midpoint.\n- **Vertex:** Outside corner, X/Y directions from the two walls below it. An inside corner is refused.\n- **Round wall / closed round rim:** Bore or Boss centre, centre and radius from the same circle fit Circular uses, at rim height. Bore vs Boss: the walls' outward normals mostly point at the axis -> Bore (a hole's wall); away -> Boss.\n- **Refused by name, op unchanged:** a face that looks down or is tilted off the axes; a bent, sloped or vertical edge; an inside corner, a corner with a sloped face, or a bottom vertex; a cone or tilted wall, or a rim that isn't round; more than one pick.\n- The Geometry tab prints the seed under the pick chip (\"Probe from the pick: Face touch toward -Z at (...)\").\n\nThe seed is written once, at the pick; generation still reads only the typed fields, so a hand edit after the pick is kept until the next pick. No project-format change (the pick is the op's existing saved selection source; the values go into the existing Probe fields). The post logic is untouched. New code is in `crates/app/src/operation/probe_pick.rs` and `probe_pick_round.rs`; `probe_op.rs` (PR #335) and all UI files are untouched.\n\n## Readings\n- `probe_pick` 9/9; `circular_pick`, `pick`, `vertex_pick`, `commands_undo`, `area_picks`, `heights_selection` all pass.\n- `a_probe_created_from_a_pick_generates_clean`: face, corner and bore probes generate with no stylus-gouge warnings.\n- Quick gate (all app suites): green except `probe_op::every_older_kind_keeps_its_stored_id_and_digest_tag`, red on main (#344 / PR #345).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Not pinned: an open curved edge (refused as \"not straight\") has no fixture; the pick doesn't check a wall is taller than the touch depth - generation's stylus check judges that.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/probe_pick.rs`)\n`a_planar_face_seeds_a_face_touch_against_its_normal`, `a_straight_top_edge_seeds_an_edge_touch_on_the_wall_under_it`, `a_vertex_seeds_an_outside_corner_from_its_two_walls`, `a_round_wall_or_rim_seeds_a_bore_or_boss_centre`, `picks_the_probe_cannot_touch_are_refused_by_name`, `the_pick_command_seeds_the_probe_and_one_undo_takes_both_back`, `a_probe_created_from_a_pick_generates_clean`, `other_kinds_are_not_seeded`, `an_inside_corner_is_refused_and_an_outside_one_on_the_l_seeds`\n\n## GUI check (why this stays a draft)\n1. Add a Probe op; on its Geometry tab set \"Click selects\" to Faces and click the top face: Find / Touch toward / Expected contact switch to Face, -Z and the face centroid, and the seed line appears under the chip.\n2. Repeat with Edges on a top edge, Vertices on an outside corner, Faces on a bore wall: Edge / Outside corner / Bore centre with its radius.\n3. Ctrl+Z once restores both the source and the previous values.\n4. Clicking the underside face shows \"geometry selection not updated: ... looks down ...\".\nPosted probe programs now carry the picked target/mode/directions; worth one Hub run of a seeded probe before merging.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/171-probe-from-pick.md`.\n\nChangelog: A Probe op seeds from one pick: a face gives a Face touch, a straight top edge an Edge touch, a vertex an outside Corner, a round wall or rim a Bore or Boss centre; picks it can't touch are refused by name\n\nFixes #171\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
